question:
Problem 3: Let $p$ be a fixed odd prime. A $p$-tuple $(a_1, a_2, \dots, a_p)$ is called good if:
(i) $0 \leq a_i \leq p-1$ for all $i$;
(ii) $a_1 + a_2 + \dots + a_p$ is not divisible by $p$;
(iii) $a_1a_2 + a_2a_3 + \dots + a_pa_1$ is divisible by $p$.
Determine the number of good $p$-tuples.

