In polar coordinates: $z = r$, so volume is:
\begin{align*}
\text{Vol} &= \iint_D r dA = \int_{-\pi/2}^{\pi/4} d\theta \int_0^{2\cos\theta} r^{2} dr \\
&= \int_{-\pi/2}^{\pi/4} \frac{(2\cos\theta)^{3}}{3} d\theta = \frac{8}{3} \int_{-\pi/2}^{\pi/4} \cos^{3}\theta d\theta \\
&= \frac{8}{3} \int_{-\pi/2}^{\pi/4} \cos\theta(1 - \sin^{2}\theta) d\theta \\
&= \frac{8}{3} [\sin\theta - \frac{\sin^{3}\theta}{3}]_{-\pi/2}^{\pi/4} \\
&= \frac{8}{3} \left[\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} - \frac{1}{6\sqrt{2}}\right) - (-1 + \frac{1}{3})\right] = \frac{40}{18}\sqrt{2} + \frac{16}{9}
\end{align*}

