Let $X \sim \text{Gamma}(\alpha, \lambda)$. The Gamma distribution has PDF:
$$
f(x) = \frac{\lambda e^{-\lambda x} (\lambda x)^{\alpha - 1}}{\Gamma(\alpha)}, \quad x \ge 0.
$$
Then the expectation and variance are known to be:
\begin{align*}
E(X) &= \frac{\alpha}{\lambda} \\
\text{Var}(X) &= \frac{\alpha}{\lambda^{2}}
\end{align*}

Use the Gamma PDF:
$$
f(x) = \frac{\lambda e^{-\lambda x} (\lambda x)^{\alpha - 1}}{\Gamma(\alpha)}
$$
Here $\lambda = \frac{1}{2}$, $\alpha = 4$, so:
\begin{align*}
P(2 < X < 4) &= \int_2^{4} \frac{1}{2} e^{-x/2} (x/2)^{3} \cdot \frac{1}{\Gamma(4)} dx \\
&= \frac{1}{24} \int_2^{4} x^{3} e^{-x/2} dx \\
&= \frac{1}{96} \int_2^{4} x^{3} e^{-x/2} dx \approx 0.1239
\end{align*}

We use the cumulative distribution:
\begin{align*}
P(X > 3) &= 1 - P(X < 3) \\
&= 1 - \frac{3^{2}}{\Gamma(2)} \int_0^{3} x e^{-3x} dx \\
&= 1 - 0.9988 = 0.001234
\end{align*}

We compute the moment directly:
